Enterprise-Grade Cryptographic Governance, Policy Engine & Audit Platform

Objective

Design, implement, and integrate a new enterprise-grade module called Cryptographic Governance Center™ into the existing QGuard Helix Platform.

This is NOT another scanner.

This is the enterprise governance layer that sits above all cryptographic discovery, quantum readiness assessments, migration planning, compliance validation, and cryptographic operations.

Every cryptographic decision throughout the platform must become governed, approved, signed, auditable, immutable, searchable, and explainable.

Core Vision

QGuard Helix must evolve from

"We detect cryptography."

to

"We govern enterprise cryptography."

Every cryptographic decision should answer:

Who approved this?
Why was it approved?
Which policy approved it?
Which compliance framework requires it?
When was it changed?
Who changed it?
What evidence supports it?
Can auditors verify it independently?
Is it still compliant today?
Has the signature remained valid?

Every answer must be cryptographically verifiable.

