Final Goal

Deliver a production-ready, enterprise-grade Cryptographic Governance Center™ that transforms QGuard Helix from a platform that merely discovers cryptography into one that governs, enforces, and proves every cryptographic decision across the enterprise.

The implementation should follow modern enterprise architecture principles (domain-driven design, event-driven workflows where appropriate, immutable audit records, multi-tenant SaaS security, and API-first integration). Every governance action—from policy creation to algorithm approval, exception handling, compliance validation, and migration decisions—must produce cryptographically verifiable evidence using ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) for digital signatures, SHA3-512 for integrity, and trusted timestamps, ensuring organizations can demonstrate governance, compliance, and post-quantum readiness with confidence.